  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "tail-envelope-failure-precedence",
      "status": "FIXED",
      "before": "The first optimized basic_interval validated/sorted replicates before encoding alpha/2. With valid 8192-bit alpha and simultaneously invalid replicates, the previous RESOURCE_GAP was replaced by a list or EVALUATION_GAP error.",
      "after": "The public wrapper preflights the original alpha/2 numeric envelope before parsing draws. The internal interval helper retains the original probability, quantile and reflected-endpoint encoding bounds.",
      "independent_counterexamples": [
        "empty list",
        "one undefined replicate",
        "20000 replicate entries"
      ],
      "qualification": "This preservation issue was identified during implementation and confirmed by an independent three-subcase red test before the correction."
    }
  ],
  "remaining_substantiated_production_blockers": [],
  "reviewed_invariants": [
    "Every input replicate is read and validated before a quantile endpoint can be selected, including late invalid and non-normalized rationals. Input list/length and canonical rational bounds remain enforced.",
    "The private ordered snapshot is a detached immutable tuple of Fractions, local to one call. There is no cross-input/result cache, float conversion or skipped replicate.",
    "Type-7 interpolation, alpha/2 and 1-alpha/2 encoding, quantile encoding, reflected basic interval endpoints and the 8192-bit arithmetic envelope remain exact.",
    "Public quantile and basic_interval retain signatures; quantile_band retains its original shape gate. Undefined/incomplete diagnose inputs retain their original early NOT_ASSESSED behavior.",
    "Instrumented basic_interval orders once. diagnose orders once per sensitivity length and reuses that tuple for both rank bands and the basic interval. Across the existing bootstrap plus MC path this reduces six ordering passes per length to two.",
    "Rank bounds, tie handling, unbounded ends, boundary equality and positive/negative/nondirectional classifications are unchanged.",
    "Only two production source files differ in the benchmark. World/seed/draw generation, gzip format, retention/replay, limits and scientific acceptance thresholds are unchanged."
  ],
